              "name": "Stephen, Archbishop of Canterbury",
              "subtitle": "Named first among John's advisers",
              "body": "Named in the charter's opening lines as the reverend father at whose advice, among others, John acted — the Archbishop of Canterbury and cardinal of the holy Roman Church, traditionally credited as a key mediator between the king and the rebellious barons."
            }
